// A chaser arrives and stops, rather than grinding into the player forever.
// Without the arrival clamp, seek walks the body in and separation pushes it
// back out every tick, for as long as the chase lasts.
//
// **10.1, not 10.0.** At 10.0 the travel divides into a whole number of whole
// steps — (10.0 - 0.55) / (3.5/60) = exactly 162 — so the body lands on the
// stopping distance whether or not the last step is clamped, and deleting the
// clamp broke nothing. At 10.1 it does not divide evenly: 163 full steps leave
// 0.0417 to go, less than a step, so the 164th has to be shortened.
//
// **The golden trace is empty, and that is the assertion.** Not one contact in
// two hundred ticks. A body that arrived and then jittered would fill it.
(
    description: "A chaser arrives at exactly touching distance and stops, without ever registering a contact.",
    setup: (
        actions: [
            Place((10.1, 0.0)),
            Seek(0),
        ],
    ),
    inputs: [],
    budget: (ticks: 200),
    expect: (
        player_pos: (x: 0.0, z: 0.0, tol: 0.0001),
        contacts: 0,
        crowd_contacts: 0,
        bodies: [
            (nth: 0, seeking: true, pos: (x: 0.55, z: 0.0, tol: 0.001)),
        ],
        trace: "a_seeker_stops_where_it_touches.trace",
    ),
)
